fix(vox-cli): recompile and retry script execution if cached binary fails to launch
scale: ~25 lines across 1 files [S]

- `crates/vox-cli/src/commands/runtime/run/script.rs`: Modified the `run` function to catch `execute_binary` errors when caching is enabled. If a cached script binary fails to launch (indicating a poisoned or stale artifact), it now recompiles the script with `no_cache: true` and retries the execution once. This addresses issues where an existing cached binary might fail to launch, particularly observed on Windows with "os error 3".

